WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.020
A warehouse has 1,000 SQL models.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.830
Someone changes one.

3
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:05.455
What breaks?

4
00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:06.905
In which order do you rebuild?

5
00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:08.415
And who tests it?

6
00:00:08.435 --> 00:00:13.965
dbt answers with three things: a graph, incremental models, and tests.

7
00:00:13.985 --> 00:00:16.275
First: what does dbt do?

8
00:00:16.295 --> 00:00:17.937
You write a select statement.

9
00:00:17.957 --> 00:00:21.060
dbt wraps it and builds the table for you.

10
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.297
To use another model, you call ref.

11
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:26.470
dbt reads those calls and builds a graph.

12
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.370
So dbt knows the order.

13
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.670
And it knows what is downstream of a change.

14
00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.580
Second: do not rebuild everything each day.

15
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.265
An incremental model processes only the new rows, and merges them in.

16
00:00:39.285 --> 00:00:40.752
The trap is late data.

17
00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:44.050
A row arrives two days late, and the filter skips it.

18
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.100
So look back a few days on each run.

19
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.700
And merge on a unique key.

20
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.535
Third: catch a bad change before it ships.

21
00:00:51.555 --> 00:00:53.398
Data tests check the rows.

22
00:00:53.418 --> 00:00:55.085
Unit tests check the logic.

23
00:00:55.105 --> 00:00:57.470
A contract fixes the columns.

24
00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.820
Start with two tests on every key: unique, and not null.

25
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.280
Last: keep a big project fast.

26
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.205
In CI, build only the models that changed, and what depends on them.

27
00:01:09.225 --> 00:01:11.365
Quick recap of dbt.

28
00:01:11.385 --> 00:01:12.790
Ref builds the graph.

29
00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.365
Incremental needs a lookback.

30
00:01:14.385 --> 00:01:16.225
And test every key.

31
00:01:16.245 --> 00:01:19.345
Now start the first lesson below.
